  "worked_solution": "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{tan}\u2061(m\u2220B)=\\sqrt{3}.$ Notice that relative to $\u2220B,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{\u2015}{AC}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{\u2015}{BC}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}\u2061(m\u2220B) & =\\frac{AC}{BC} \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}(x-4)}{8-x} \\\\ \\sqrt{3}(8-x) & =\\sqrt{3}(x-4) \\\\ 8-x & =x-4 \\\\ 2x & =12 \\\\ x & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =8-x=8-6=2, \\\\ AC & =\\sqrt{3}(x-4)=\\sqrt{3}(6-4)=2\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $\u25b3ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\cdot 2\\sqrt{3} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
